    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0215" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg191"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Judd.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 66.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 9, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 11th of February, No. 56, and I give you my sincere
                    thanks for the exposition of the political and military movements of the allies
                    in the war against Denmark. Information from London of a date somewhat later
                    than yours induces a belief that some settlement of the controversy is at hand.
                    Nevertheless, this information comes through channels that are not altogether
                    reliable. The British people desire a settlement so earnestly that their
                    opinions and even their facts take a coloring from their wishes.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM EL SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman B. Judd</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Berlin.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
